WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.952
Hi! Today we go shopping.

2
00:00:06.352 --> 00:00:09.816
At the supermarket and at the market.

3
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.564
How much do you need? Listen:

4
00:00:15.964 --> 00:00:18.468
a kilo of apples

5
00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:21.204
a litre of milk

6
00:00:21.604 --> 00:00:24.372
a pack of pasta

7
00:00:24.772 --> 00:00:27.516
a can of tomatoes

8
00:00:27.916 --> 00:00:30.468
a pot of yoghurt

9
00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:36.375
Looking for something? Then you ask:

10
00:00:36.775 --> 00:00:40.575
Excuse me, where can I find rice?

11
00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:43.311
Or you ask:

12
00:00:43.711 --> 00:00:46.791
Do you have fresh strawberries?

13
00:00:47.191 --> 00:00:52.359
Say Entschuldigung (excuse me) first. That's polite.

14
00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:57.867
What do you need? Listen:

15
00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:00.675
I need milk.

16
00:01:01.075 --> 00:01:05.859
After brauchen, kaufen and haben comes the accusative:

17
00:01:06.259 --> 00:01:09.003
I need an apple.

18
00:01:09.403 --> 00:01:12.339
I buy a bag.

19
00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.171
I have a loaf of bread.

20
00:01:15.571 --> 00:01:18.195
I have no rice.

21
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.692
A tip for Germany:

22
00:01:23.092 --> 00:01:28.524
Bring your own bag. A plastic bag costs money!

23
00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:34.153
Listen: Lena is at the market.

24
00:01:34.553 --> 00:01:38.737
Hello! What would you like?

25
00:01:39.137 --> 00:01:42.601
A kilo of tomatoes, please.

26
00:01:43.001 --> 00:01:45.601
Anything else?

27
00:01:46.001 --> 00:01:49.105
How much are the strawberries?

28
00:01:49.505 --> 00:01:52.273
Three euros a kilo.

29
00:01:52.673 --> 00:01:57.433
Good, one kilo. That's all.

30
00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:06.461
Now you! What do you need today? Write a shopping list!

31
00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:20.303
Great! Now you can:

32
00:02:20.703 --> 00:02:24.911
You shop at the supermarket and at the market.

33
00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.431
See you soon!
